## React Server Components (CRITICAL)
ALWAYS default to Server Components. Only `'use client'` when necessary: interactive features (`onClick`/`onChange`/`onSubmit`), Browser APIs (`window`/`document`/`localStorage`), React hooks (`useState`/`useEffect`/`useContext`), client-side libraries, event listeners

❌ Unnecessary client components, entire page as client

## No Redundant Client Fetch When Server Data Exists
When a page fetches data on the server and passes it as props (e.g., `user`), the client component must NOT trigger a refetch. Use the prop directly. Do not call `useQuery`/data hooks when server data is provided. If a hook is needed for caching, pass `initialData` with `refetchOnMount: false` or `staleTime: Infinity` to prevent duplicate requests.

## Performance Optimization
See @.cursor/rules/frontend/react.mdc for concurrent rendering (Suspense/Transitions/Deferred Values)

### Core Web Vitals & Images
Optimize Core Web Vitals (LCP <2.5s, FID <100ms, CLS <0.1), images (WebP, proper sizes, lazy loading)
